y had there not been that vigorous  discussion so that's what we want in our  story rooms  um the flip side of that is that even as  you're disagreeing you have to be  respectful of other people's points of  view  because when you talk story  you make yourself very vulnerable  when you talk about story you're talking  about you'll end up in the story room  for hours and days on end talking about  things that you love  things that you hate  things that make you sad  and you're really pulling from your own  life experience  so when you offer an idea  to some extent you're saying this is who  i am  and that line between who you are and  what you do starts to become very fuzzy  so it's really important to find that  place where you can be honest and open  but never let things get personal  um i think we have yes we have slides  here of uh don and i  in the store go back to that other slide  real quick garth  look how exciting that is  look at that energy look at it  it's just it's amazing it's just it  really captured the raw energy look  there's that of the biggest discussion i  was touting look at it look at it  i'm very interested you should mention  because most people here i would wager  most people have never been in a disney  story room and you should very briefly  describe  why is it set up that way what is all  that stuff what's the purpose of the  pictures on top the pictures on the  bottom  oh well we usually we we've had this  convenient little space at the top of  our story rooms uh that i think back on  bolt we began the tradition of pinning  up big pieces of his dev art that would  stay up there to be a a visual  inspiration  um and the story room itself becomes a  real uh sanctuary it's a home away from  home  and and we will spend hours and days and  weeks and years on end  in this room it really is the creative  center for the story department and it  really hub and it's a hub for the whole  production  and it's where we'll work out the  outline there's the outline on the on  the back wall there all the cards uh  you'll you'll work with the story team  on the outline the outline will continue  to evolve over the course of the years  of production  you'll meet with writers and talk about  the scenes they'll often write a scene  and come back  we'll have a story artist take the scene  go off and board it and bring it back  pitch it in this room to the story team  and begin the cycle over and over and  over again of rewriting re-boarding uh  and and and restructuring the film it  all happens in this room uh and and i  should talk i should i think it's worth  mentioning  that the people who work in these kind  of environments the writers and the  story artists they have to have a very  thick skin  because often your job is to go off on  your own and work on a scene and and  create something that hopefully you like  and you think serves the film and  something you become very invested in  and after  one or two weeks of work you'll come  back into the story room and you have to  pitch it and you have to pitch it with  passion and conviction and you have to  believe in it and then you have to turn  a switch and you have to sit down and  listen to people whose job it is to  judge that idea and they'll tell you  what they like what they didn't like  what they do differently  and you have to be receptive to these  other points of view even if at first  you don't agree  um because it in that in that conflict  you may find that third and better idea  um and all of this iteration all of this  rewriting rebording it's all sort of  working towards a screening there's  always a screening looming  and our screenings are are a real  milestone for the production we'll do  between six and maybe eight or nine at  the most screenings  and who's in these screenings who is  sitting in these it's it's the crew  we'll cut it's all internal the crew  will come and watch it we'll often times  invite people in from other shows just  to get a fresh perspective  and and that's what it really is really  it's an opportunity to take stock of  where you're at on the film  you know bob eye girls show up allen  horn we'll have the big boys there we'll  also have uh you know the the marketing  teams come in just so that they can  start getting um you know it really is a  chance for us to all invest in what this  film is going to be
 

